  "case": "render.layout.io-round-half-even",
  "clause": "DESIGN R3.3 \u00a79.4 Region geometry, including Process IO",
  "witness": "rational computations round once at output, ties to even",
  "derivation": "In_A DI 36.001 x 50.003 -> 36001 x 50003 ticks; left = 150000 - 36001/2 = 131999.5 -> 132000 (even); RH = max(80000, 50003 + 20000) = 80000, A = B = 25001.5, cy = max(25001.5, 40000) = 40000, y = 40000 - 50003/2 = 14998.5 -> 14998 (even); exact right 168000.5 (+20000 gap) does not collide with In_B at 332000 (y 15000). Only In_A and In_B are placed; Out_C keeps its transcribed DI geometry with role shape. Row rule (spec \u00a74.3): items in \u00a77.2 placement order; footprint max(object, label) width; left = anchor centre - footprint/2 when the anchor is shown, else contentLeft or previous right + gap; clamp to contentLeft; collision shifts right; one row at the top of the support body [Ly, Ly+RH], RH = max(minHeight, max(object+label) + 2 padding) (harmonization K2); every object centre lies on one line cy = Ly + max(A, (RH + A - B)/2), A = max h/2, B = max(h/2 + label height), so the union of the stacks is centred in the row (DESIGN \u00a79.4 'align centers on one IO row'); exact rationals, one roundEven per output coordinate. The profile is re-pinned to the lot-4 extension packages neutral-render-descriptors/1 and neutral-render-base/1 (tests/profile_render/expected/artifacts/), which admit every native type of the tree.",
